<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec service price index falls 0.7% yr/yr-BOJ.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec service price index falls 0.7% yr/yr-BOJ.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corporate service price index (CSPI) fell 0.7 percent in December from a year earlier, and fell 0.3 percent from a month earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The overall index stood at 101.6 for December. The index tracks price movements in the service industry and uses 1990 as its base year.  </p>
<p>The following are percentage changes in components of the index year-on-year (Y-Y) and month-on-month (M-M):</p>
<p>			DEC Y-Y    M-M	 NOV  Y-Y   M-M</p>
<p> Finance/Insurance     -0.2  0.0	    -0.2  0.0</p>
<p> Real estate	     -1.8  0.0	    -1.6  0.0</p>
<p> Transport		 -0.4 -0.5	    +0.1 -0.3</p>
<p> Information services   0.0  0.0	     0.0  0.0</p>
<p> Communications	  -1.2 -0.1	    -1.2 -0.1</p>
<p> Advertising services  +1.5 -1.0	    +1.5 +0.6</p>
<p> Lease/rental services -5.2 -0.3	    -5.7 -0.1</p>
<p> Other services	  +0.5  0.0	    +0.6 +0.1</p>
<p>Percentage annual changes in components of the index year-on-year:</p>
<p>				  calendar 1996	calendar 1995</p>
<p> Finance/Insurance	     +0.1		    +1.2</p>
<p> Real estate		     +2.4		    -3.1</p>
<p> Transport			 +0.7		    +0.5</p>
<p> Information services	  -0.3		    -3.3</p>
<p> Communications		  -1.7		    +0.4</p>
<p> Advertising services	  +1.3		    +1.0</p>
<p> Lease/rental services	 -5.8		    -6.1</p>
<p> Other services		  +0.1		    -0.3</p>
</text>
